  "form": "Problem note",
  "pages": 21,
  "question": "Which growth rates force irrational reciprocal sums, and which additional tail conditions force the Sylvester recurrence?",
  "precis": "For strictly increasing positive integers with a_n²/a_{n+1}=1+3/n+o(n^{-3}), the reciprocal sum is irrational. The argument extracts a cubic polynomial from an integer tail numerator, restricts its coefficients using a square in a cubic field, and excludes the remaining cases modulo seven. Under rationality and the quadratic growth limit, separate criteria using bounded numerator increases and weighted first crossings force the eventual Sylvester recurrence. The unrestricted Erdős–Graham question remains open.",
  "owns": "cubic-rate irrationality, nonintegral regular-rate exclusion and sufficient tail criteria for the Sylvester recurrence; the unrestricted Erdős–Graham question remains open",
